<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sengge Namgyal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1642</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sengge Namgyal was king of Ladakh in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himalayas">Himalayas</a> from about 1616 to 1642, the greatest ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namgyal-dynasty">Namgyal dynasty</a>. He expanded his kingdom into western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>, conquering Guge, and built the royal palace at Leh. A patron of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibetan-buddhism">Tibetan Buddhism</a>, he supported the lama Taktsang Repa and the founding of Hemis monastery, the largest in Ladakh.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sengge-namgyal.jpg" alt="Sengge Namgyal" width="320" height="381" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aizwal · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mural_of_King_Sengge_Namgyal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
